From 7fbab996b019b2b85747216774704df123bf0542 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: test <test@test.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 05:37:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] RISC-V: add Zbc-accelerated crc64

Add a carry-less-multiply (clmul/clmulh) crc64 implementation for
RISC-V (rv64gc_zbc_zbb), the hot checksum path for RDB/AOF persistence:

  - src/crc64_riscv.c (new): 128-bit 4-way parallel folding + per-lane
    merge using scalar Zbc clmul/clmulh, with a local slice-by-8
    fallback for short (<128B) inputs. Bit-exact with crcspeed.
  - src/crc64.c: dispatch to crc64_riscv at runtime when /proc/cpuinfo
    reports zbc (cached); otherwise keep the crcspeed path unchanged.
  - src/Makefile: build crc64_riscv.c with -march=rv64gc_zbc_zbb and
    -fno-lto (per-TU arch can not go through LTO).

Correctness: official crc64Test vectors pass (e9c6d914c4b8d9ca and
c7794709e69683b3), plus randomized/chained/boundary checks against the
slice-by-8 reference. Performance on Spacemit X100 (k3), vs slice-by-8
crcspeed (official crc64Test --crc, M/sec):

    len      baseline crcspeed    PR-A Zbc      speedup
    256 B       1084              ~1800         ~1.7x
    1 KiB       1070              ~2700         ~2.5x
    4 KiB       1129              ~2850         ~2.5x
    64 KiB      1109              ~2900         ~2.6x
    128 KiB     1111              ~2900         ~2.6x

Zbc is ~2.6x at 64 KiB..128 KiB; buffers <128 B intentionally keep the
slice-by-8 path (fold setup overhead exceeds gains).
No behavior change on non-RISC-V or Zbc-less builds.
